The lobby stub needs enet's include path.

With --without-lobby the lobby project still compiles lobby/scripting, and that
reaches enet.h through the network headers - but its extern_libs list names only
spidermonkey, boost, libsodium and fmt. Nobody notices on the other platforms,
because there enet's headers sit in a default include path: a distribution puts
them in /usr/include, and the Android port's compiler wrapper adds -isystem over
the whole Termux prefix. Here they are in libraries/macos/enet/include and
nowhere else, so the list has to say so.

    source/lib/external_libraries/enet.h:48:10: fatal error: 'enet/enet.h' file not found

--- build/premake/premake5.lua
+++ build/premake/premake5.lua
@@ -804,6 +804,12 @@
 		extern_libs = {
 			"spidermonkey",
 			"boost",
+			-- lobby/scripting reaches enet.h through the network headers even
+			-- with the lobby switched off. Every other platform gets away
+			-- without this because enet's headers sit in a default include
+			-- path; here they are in libraries/macos/enet, so the list has to
+			-- say so.
+			"enet",
 			"libsodium",
 			"fmt",
 		}
